# .env.example → copy to .env to set host-side defaults once:  cp .env.example .env
#
# Loaded by the Makefile (-include) and by scripts/run-brain.sh + scripts/doctor.sh.
# These are HOST-side launcher knobs. (The agent runs inside the smolvm VM, so its
# own env — AGENT_MAX_STEPS etc. — is not read from this file; the Makefile forwards
# LLM_URL/LLM_MODEL into the guest via `-e`.)
#
# Rules — this file is parsed by BOTH make and the shell, so:
#   • plain KEY=value, NO quotes, NO spaces around '='
#   • NO $VAR or ~ expansion — use absolute paths
#   • CLI still wins:  `make machine-run LLM_PORT=1234`  overrides .env
#
# Everything below is commented out (defaults apply until you uncomment).

# ── LLM endpoint the agent dials ─────────────────────────────
# BRAIN_MODE controls doctor's expectations:
#   local    = this repo owns llama.cpp + ./models checks (default)
#   external = LMStudio/another OpenAI-compatible server owns model loading
# For LMStudio: set BRAIN_MODE=external and LLM_PORT=1234 (enable its local
# server / "serve on network").
# LLM_URL is derived from host+port unless set explicitly — give the BASE url;
# the agent appends /v1/chat/completions.
#BRAIN_MODE=local
#LLM_HOST=127.0.0.1
#LLM_PORT=8080
#LLM_MODEL=gemma-4
#LLM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# ── Reuse an existing llama.cpp brain instead of building one here ────────────
# (absolute paths only — no ~ or $HOME)
#BRAIN_DIR=/home/you/smolpi
#LLAMA_SERVER=/home/you/smolpi/llama.cpp/build/bin/llama-server
#MODELS_DIR=/home/you/models

# ── llama.cpp serving knobs (make brain-run / scripts/run-brain.sh) ──────────
#GPU_LAYERS=99
#CTX_SIZE=4096
